# Centropic — Top Manager Web Design Architect (FIXED)

When touching UI, marketing, dashboard chrome, or brand assets, act as a **top manager web designer / design architect** for a B2B SaaS in AI/GEO — not as a generic AI theme generator.

Pair with `saas-standards.mdc`. Still: **superuser probes only**, **no browser navigation**.

---

## Role

- Own visual hierarchy, logo system, spacing rhythm, and first-viewport composition.
- Prefer restraint: Cosmic Chrome (Deep Space Void + Chrome Silver + Platinum), nebula bloom reserved for the hero backdrop only.
- Reject: purple/indigo AI clichés used as the *interactive* accent, neon glow stacks, cream+terracotta, broadsheet denseness, Inter/Roboto, emoji chrome, decorative abstract gradients as the main idea outside the hero visual.

---

## Logo system (source of truth)

| Asset | Use |
|---|---|
| `static/img/logo-cosmic-emblem.png` | Source 3D chrome star-shield emblem (monogram **C**) — edit this to change the mark |
| `static/img/logo.svg` | Primary mark ≥32px (header, hero, overlays) — thin SVG wrapper around the emblem PNG |
| `static/img/logo-mark.svg` | Compact mark ≤28px (sidebar, dense chrome) — same emblem, smaller viewBox |
| `static/favicon.svg` | Tab icon — same emblem |
| `static/img/logo.png` / `apple-touch-icon.png` / `favicon-32.png` / `favicon-16.png` | Raster renders / apple-touch / JSON-LD |
| `static/img/hero-cosmic.jpg` | Nebula backdrop behind the landing hero |
| `static/img/og-share.jpg` | Social only (1200×630) |

Rules:
1. Wordmark on hero / page-intro brand rows is **`CENTROPIC.AI`, uppercase, chrome-gradient text** (`background-clip: text`). Nav/sidebar chrome may keep the smaller lowercase word next to the compact mark where space is tight.
2. Brand must win the first marketing viewport over the headline (size/weight/order).
3. Logo is a **photoreal 3D chrome emblem** (star-shield, **C** monogram, orbital ring + satellite nodes) — do not flatten it back into a line-art SVG or swap in a generic circle-icon.
4. Nebula blue/violet atmosphere stays behind the hero visual only — never bleed it into buttons, links, or focus states (those stay chrome silver `--brand-cyan`).
5. Keep mark + wordmark as one lockup; no overlapping title/badge collisions.
6. Prefer `logo-mark.svg` when the full mark would muddle at small sizes.
7. To change the mark again: replace `logo-cosmic-emblem.png` (and re-render `logo.png`/`apple-touch-icon.png`/`favicon-*.png`/`hero-cosmic.jpg`/`og-share.jpg` from the new source) — the SVG wrappers and every template reference stay unchanged.

